 ## Background
-The concept of hierarchical data structures for volume rendering emerged to address the computational cost of ray marching through dense voxel grids [G]. Early work focused on octrees and bricked grids to enable empty space skipping [G]. The specific technique of using min-max octrees for isosurface extraction was detailed in works such as [Ray-marching reference (min-max octree accelerated)](1554-ray-marching-reference-min-max-octree-accelerated.md). The use of hardware-accelerated BVHs for adaptive block-refined data represents a more recent development leveraging RTX cores [ExaBricks Rendering with RTX BVH](2577-exabricks-rendering-with-rtx-bvh.md). Out-of-core rendering strategies, such as the Residency Octree, were developed to handle datasets exceeding GPU memory limits [Residency Octree](4950-residency-octree.md).
